# Machine-readable derivative of docs/records/agent-verification.md.
# Passed to `docker compose` as --env-file (see feature plan criterion 4).
# The smoke check asserts this file agrees with the human record — a
# hand-edit to either is caught, not silently shipped.

CLAUDE_VERSION=2.1.260
CLAUDE_SOURCE=npm:@anthropic-ai/claude-code@2.1.260

CODEX_VERSION=0.152.1
CODEX_SOURCE=npm:@openai/codex@0.152.1

# agy has no version-pinning flag (agent-verification.md). Pinned instead by
# direct, checksum-verified download of the manifest-resolved artifact for
# linux_arm64 (Docker Desktop on Apple silicon, A1) -- see
# docs/records/agent-verification.md, "agy version pin -- resolved".
AGY_VERSION=1.1.26
AGY_SOURCE=https://storage.googleapis.com/antigravity-public/antigravity-cli/1.1.26-5550154686791680/linux-arm/cli_linux_arm64.tar.gz
AGY_URL=https://storage.googleapis.com/antigravity-public/antigravity-cli/1.1.26-5550154686791680/linux-arm/cli_linux_arm64.tar.gz
AGY_SHA512=332dddb06ab4d901a44cfd4b9b358848230e64a64515a8e79b03822348adac9ce92d54cb4fc5119ef075edfba922820c926dfddf82d3a49f4ecdb6e6704dfc75

# Mediator image pins (01.3 SF-4). Machine-readable derivative of
# docs/records/mediator-selection.md, which verified P1-P8 against exactly this
# build. Both halves matter: Debian point releases supersede in place, so an
# unpinned install moves off the verified build while the version-scoped Squid
# directives keep parsing. The smoke check asserts the squid pin and the base
# digest agree with the record.
MEDIATOR_BASE_DIGEST=sha256:d7e12182ce18b85b93007c1dedf31f2d29e01ccf3182cc4017c709b6259bc132
SQUID_VERSION=6.13-2+deb13u2

# unbound is the resolver binary SF-5 configures. Not verified by SF-1 -- SF-1's
# properties are the proxy's -- so it is pinned here but not asserted against the
# selection record.
UNBOUND_VERSION=1.22.0-2+deb13u3

# The pod's DNS policy engine (01.3 SF-5). unbound stays as the RE-ORIGINATING
# half; dnsdist is the policy half in front of it. The split is a verified
# necessity, not a preference -- docs/records/resolver-verification.md shows
# unbound alone cannot express criterion 4's exact-name, QTYPE or 0x20 terms, and
# dnsdist alone forwards the client's EDNS options verbatim.
DNSDIST_VERSION=1.9.16-0+deb13u1

# yq reads the resolved policy artifact so the mediator's configuration is
# GENERATED from it rather than hand-written (SC-6). The image had no YAML parser
# before this sub-feature; SF-6's proxy render and SF-7's stage-1 schema check both
# inherit this one.
#
# Pinned by checksum rather than by an apt version, for the reason AGY_SHA512
# exists: Debian's `yq` is a Python wrapper that would put an interpreter inside
# the enforcement point, where this is a single static binary. Both architectures
# are pinned so the image is not silently host-specific.
YQ_VERSION=v4.47.2
YQ_SHA256_ARM64=05df1f6aed334f223bb3e6a967db259f7185e33650c3b6447625e16fea0ed31f
YQ_SHA256_AMD64=1bb99e1019e23de33c7e6afc23e93dad72aad6cf2cb03c797f068ea79814ddb0

# jq reads each agent's own transcript line and assembles the action-log JSON
# (02.1 SF-2, images/recorder/Dockerfile). Measured against MEDIATOR_BASE_DIGEST
# with `apt-cache policy jq` rather than guessed -- Debian point releases supersede
# in place, same reasoning as SQUID_VERSION above.
JQ_VERSION=1.7.1-6+deb13u3

# The pinned Debian snapshot the agent images install OS packages from (01.5 SF-5,
# R7.18, Edge Case 8). A SNAPSHOT, NOT A SUITE: `bookworm` plus name=version resolves
# today and fails after the next archive rotation, and SC-8 measures precisely the
# clean rebuild that happens later.
#
# These duplicate `package_repository.apt` in profiles/*.yaml, and the duplication is
# deliberate and CHECKED. The `agent-base` stage is profile-independent -- it is what
# SF-6 publishes to GHCR -- so it cannot read a profile without making the published
# base vary per profile, contradicting D10. It therefore takes its own pins here. The
# divergence that would matter is caught mechanically: agent-base records the archive
# it used at /etc/agent-apt-snapshot-url, and images/pack-install.sh refuses the build
# if the profile names a different one.
#
# SNAPSHOT_FINGERPRINT is the trust anchor, asserted at build via gpgv's VALIDSIG line
# against images/keyrings/debian-archive.gpg -- a key substitution fails the build.
SNAPSHOT_URL=https://snapshot.debian.org/archive/debian/20260901T000000Z/
SNAPSHOT_SUITE=bookworm
SNAPSHOT_FINGERPRINT=B8B80B5B623EAB6AD8775C45B7C5D7D6350947F8

# `git` is installed in the agent-base stage rather than supplied by a pack (feature
# plan Deviation 2): R2.9's host_git_config mount and scripts/scrub-gitconfig.sh are
# profile-level features, and they are inert without a git binary. The SHA-256 is the
# .deb hash read from the SIGNED Packages index of the snapshot above; git-man comes
# in as a dependency and rides the same signed chain (Deviation 13).
GIT_VERSION=1:2.39.5-0+deb12u3
GIT_SHA256=435176549a9f5c8bbadaa126b64a036b38ea34ad9f3eb128dc40b8407a5b5620

# The CI-published agent-base, consumed by digest (01.5 SF-6b, D21, R10.2). NO DEFAULT
# in images/Dockerfile: unset, the FROM expands to `...@` and the build fails on an
# invalid reference rather than resolving to a mutable tag.
#
# THIS LINE IS A REVIEWED EDIT, not a generated one. It is copied by a human from the
# agent-sandbox-image workflow's run summary, which is Edge Case 11's bootstrap: the
# Dockerfile pins a digest that does not exist until the workflow has run once, so the
# first publish comes from the working branch and its digest is committed here.
#
# It is the INDEX digest -- one linux/arm64 manifest plus the SBOM and provenance
# attestation manifests -- not the platform manifest, so the attestations stay reachable
# from what is pinned. Verified anonymously against ghcr.io at the time of the edit:
# the index carries https://spdx.dev/Document (4,165,960 bytes) and
# https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1 (119,577 bytes).
#
# Published by run 34376295042 from commit bdabf72. The base is linux/arm64 ONLY --
# feature plan Deviation 15 records why that is mechanism and not preference.
AGENT_BASE_DIGEST=sha256:213d56ab12d0f4bb945f3a7f2b808c4e2b52fe18d24d9624c23e59d09006f9b3
